I'm using the standard American QWERTY keyboard, and my armor always
ends up looking like this for easy strippage/redressing.  I know about
the "A" command, but for some reason, I still prefer this:
E - Helmet
R - Gloves
T - Shoes
Y - Robe/Cloak
U - Body Armor
I - T-Shirt
O - Shield
This is so that I can quickly go back and forth across the top row
without having to release the shift key.  The same with my primary
rings, on P and L.  And my main amulet(s) on M and J.
of the other things, my starting weapon usually stays on a, but my
artifact weapon usually gets put to w.  Other things that have started
to filter themselves out:
f - pickaxe (holdover from before I discovered autodig a few weeks
ago.)
t - towel/blindfold
k - key
h - bag of holding
g- oilskin/other bag
d - lifesaving corpse
y - rubber chicken (j/k)
x - rubber chicken (for real this time)
y - lamp (not quitting because I want to throw my lamp!)
t - thrown ammunition
r - quivered ammunition
n - unihorn
s - !oFH (only when going into combat)
e - b?oRC (end-game combat)
I then try to get my luckstone on the upper-case somewhere, and fill
the rest of my inventory with #named worthless pieces of glass when
encountering titans, liches, unhappy priests and the like and during
the two ascension runs I've been on.
My wands, especially cancel, will usually go to the bottom row, lower
case.  The only rule I've got for this is don't put any of them near
the "." key.  I've learned from too many problems the value of keeping
the /oCancel out of any container.  You never know when you're gonna
want to make harmless a nymph or trice or something.
